have run the examples yourself.  ## If you are blocked  Do not fake progress. Write what you tried, the exact error, and what you believe is required into `FINDINGS.md`, then stop.  A blocked phase with an honest report is worth more than a green phase with a lie in it. `verify.sh` will reject the phase anyway; a fabrication only adds a blocking review finding on top.  --- ## RESUMED WORK — read this before touching anything A previous attempt's work is already merged into your tree. DO NOT start over and DO NOT rewrite it from scratch. Your job is to finish what is missing:  1. Run the four gates FIRST, before changing anything, to see the current state. 2. Read phases/phase-075/REPORT.md from the previous attempt (harvested below if    present) to see what it claimed and what the gate actually said. 3. Fix exactly what failed. Add what is missing. Do not remove working code.  ### Previous REPORT.md (do not trust its gate claims — verify them)  ``` # Phase 075 — Teach the language server navigation: goto-definition, references, completion  ## What changed  | File | Lines | What | |---|---|---| | src/lsp.rs | +1005 −1 | `Location`, `Definition`, `DefinitionKind`; token-level lexical scope walk; `goto_definition`, `find_references`, `completions` and their JSON forms; greedy string-literal and `//` comment context checks; balanced `else if`, multi-name `set`, typed/`of` parameters, catch binders, object-only `has`, range `to` recognition, decorator-position checks, and function-literal frames that close where the parsed one-line body ends | | src/lsp.rs | +115 −31 | resumed run: `DeclarationSink` removes the clippy `too_many_arguments` failure without an `allow` suppression, then the review fixes: an assignment `to` is no longer a literal opener, object members resolve in the deferred pass, lexer errors keep their span, string/comment delimiters count as inside, builtin references exclude member/type names, goto excludes member names, and CR/CRLF line starts and comm