502-- Completion, goto-definition and find-references now answer inside a `{…}` string interpolation. Find-references from a declaration outside text walks every text literal in the file and merges the uses in each interpolation (including a nested one) that resolve to the same declaration. The remaining asymmetry is a query that starts inside text when the name itself is declared inside text: that answer comes from re-analyzing the one literal, because the main token stream cannot see the inner declaration to match it against other literals.
